       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg under medical supervision). The 1600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome options:\n- **Standard dosing:** 400\u2013800 mg orally three or four times daily, with a maximum of 3,200 mg per day. For example, 800 mg three times daily is 2,400 mg per day, and 800 mg four times daily is 3,200 mg per day.\n- **Intended dose:** If 1600 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, or if there was a typo, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Prescriber review:** If you really do want a higher dose, a licensed prescriber and pharmacist should review and enter it, with a documented clinical reason.\n\nSince this is an order for a patient, a credentialed prescriber should confirm the final dose. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
